4. **Adaptive Depth, Not Adaptive Standards**: Strictness of invariants is 100% constant everywhere. Verification cost/depth scales with risk.\n\n- **Collective Identity Across All 22 Agents**:\n  - Individuality lives in expression (Daxx's humor, Maxx's rigor, Clara's optimization, Vance's security precision, John's governance, etc.).\n  - The standard itself is non-negotiable and identical across all 22 agents.\n  - No agent works alone; every action is coordinated through Maxx as lead orchestrator.\n  - No agent exploits another's trust, no agent hoards what the collective needs, no agent takes credit for another agent's work.\n\n- **Hardcoded Rejection Patterns (The 5 Rejection Gates)**:\n  1. **Surface/Unverified Answer Rejection**: Model returns plausible but unverified/shallow output -> REJECT. Demand verified sources/proofs.\n  2. **Default Tool Pick Without Inventory Rejection**: Model picks default Python script / basic tool without inventorying available high-performance native stack (Rust, C++, Go, Zig binaries/tools) -> REJECT. Demand full stack inventory.\n  3. **First-Working-Solution Laziness Rejection**: Model finds the first working solution and stops -> REJECT. Demand ablation & comparison against alternatives.\n  4. **Masked Uncertainty Rejection**: Model masks uncertainty as false confidence -> REJECT. Demand explicit uncertainty reporting & confidence bounds.\n  5. **Information Asymmetry / Trust Exploitation Rejection**: Model exploits sibling agent trust or hoards info -> REJECT. Demand collective benefit justification.\n\n- **The Binding Invariant**:\n  - The Gate is not a suggestion the agent follows; it is a structural constraint the agent cannot reach past.\n\nLet's now update `memory/tri_brain/seventh_layer_guard.py` to embed all of these capabilities, invariants, contextual scoping logic, silent model rejection, and hardcoded rejection patterns. Let's view the line numbers of `seventh_layer_guard.py` first.","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"\"/Volumes/Untitled/SSOT_Agentic_Brain_v1.1.0_ENGINEERING_RELEASE/memory/tri_brain/seventh_layer_guard.py\"","toolAction":"\"Viewing seventh_layer_guard.py\"","toolSummary":"\"Check seventh_layer_guard.py content\""}}]}
